[open] PR #11: fix(resolver): find TypeScript's lib files in TypeScript 7's platform package
  castrog
  OPEN | [ok]
  Checks: 14/15 passed
  https://github.com/orin-dx/oxc-react-docgen/pull/11

  #8 moved `main` to TypeScript 7.0.2, which broke `test_indexed_access_into_ambient_dom_interface_resolves_via_real_lib` in Test and Coverage on every PR (#9, #10).

  It's a real product bug, not a test issue: TS 7 ships `lib.dom.d.ts`/`lib.es5.d.ts` in the installed `@typescript/typescript-<platform>` optional dependency, and both packages' `exports` hide `./lib`. `typescript/lib/lib.dom.d.ts` no longer resolves, so DOM/ES globals (`HTMLDivElement["dir"]`, `Date`, …) silently stopped resolving for any user on TS 7.

  Fix: when `typescript/lib/*` doesn't resolve, read `typescript/package.json`, resolve its installed `@typescript/typescript-*` optional dependency's `package.json` (the only exported path), and use that package's `lib/`.

  Tests: hermetic TS ≤ 6 and TS 7 layouts (TS 7 with one of two platforms installed and `exports` hiding `./lib`), plus no-TypeScript. Disabling the fallback fails the TS 7 test and the real-lib pipeline test.

